        "articleSummary": "Streptococcus agalactiae serotype Ib/ST261 has emerged as the dominant bullfrog pathogen causing high mortality in Hainan, China, from 2019–2023. Virulence gene profile remains stable across 2019 and 2023 isolates: pavA + sip + iagA + cfb + hylB + bibA + cspA + fbsA. Resistance-associated mutations persist: gyrA (S81L), parC (D83Y), pbp1A (Y305F, A604T, N639S), pbp2B (V79A, S247F, S313P, N412D, T656I). Despite consistently high phenotypic resistance to tetracycline (97%), chloramphenicol (92%), cotrimoxazole (92%), sulfamethoxazole (90%), and penicillin (90%), acquired resistance genes tetM, aacC2, sul1, sul2 were largely lost. Environmental stress from 2019 to 2023 coincided with pronounced AMR shifts: imipenem resistance up fourfold; spectinomycin, streptomycin, and amikacin resistance increased 34-, 46-, and 49.7-fold, respectively. Biofilm formation remains weak, underscoring persistent virulence and multidrug resistance that challenge treatment of bullfrog bacteremia in aquaculture.",
