        "articleSummary": "Measles cases declined in week 9 of 2026, from 511 to 231, according to Acting Director General of Disease Prevention and Control Andi Saguni. The reduction is attributed to targeted immunization measures across affected areas, including outbreak response immunization (ORI) implemented in all districts and cities experiencing a measles outbreak (KLB), followed by intensified immunization in areas with rising cases. While overall numbers fall, authorities remain vigilant for high-incidence areas such as Bima Regency and Bima City in West Nusa Tenggara Province (NTB). Cumulatively through week 9 of 2026, there were 10,826 suspected measles cases, 8,716 laboratory-confirmed cases, and 45 outbreaks across 11 provinces. The decline reflects accurate immunization deployment and strengthened risk communications, information, and education (KIE) to the public.",
