        "articleSummary": "As of March 15, 2026, measles outbreaks in Indonesia include a measles emergency declared in Riau province. Indonesia ranks second globally in measles outbreak cases, with 72 child deaths from measles-related complications reported. Measles is highly contagious via airborne transmission, and Eid al-Fitr/mudik gatherings pose high risk, especially for children under five not fully vaccinated, immunocompromised individuals, and pregnant women. Early symptoms resemble flu: high fever, cough, runny nose, and conjunctivitis, followed by rash. RS Awal Bros urges parents to seek medical care promptly if a child develops high fever with a rash, to enable early diagnosis and management; severe cases may include breathing difficulties, ear pain, diarrhea, or dehydration. Preventive measures include MR/MMR vaccination: first dose at 9 months, boosters at 18 months and 5–7 years; maintain hand hygiene, masks, and good nutrition. The hospital network offers vaccination services and pediatric consultations ahead of the homecoming period.",
