        "articleSummary": "Six confirmed measles cases detected in Pati Regency, East Java, Indonesia, in early 2026, across three subdistricts: Tayu (4), Tambakromo (1), and Sukolilo (1). Most patients are children under 10 years old. Common symptoms include high fever (38–40°C), persistent cough, runny nose, and red, light-sensitive eyes, with fatigue and poor appetite. After several days, a red rash appears, typically starting behind the ears and face and spreading to the neck, body, arms, and legs. Koplik spots may be present in the mouth. Health authorities urge prompt medical evaluation to prevent wider transmission. Preventive measures emphasize hand hygiene, cough and sneeze etiquette, and avoiding direct contact with cases. Vaccination with MR or MMR is the most effective prevention; many patients reportedly had not received measles immunization, and vaccination campaigns via Pati’s community health centers are ongoing to close immunity gaps.",
