        "articleSummary": "As of 15 March 2026, Samarinda City Health Office in East Kalimantan reports 72 suspected measles cases, up from 62, with all samples undergoing laboratory testing at a reference lab. No laboratory-confirmed measles cases have been reported yet; status remains 'suspected' pending lab validation to confirm positivity. The majority of suspected cases involve children, many of whom are unvaccinated. Samarinda has not declared a Public Health Emergency of Outbreak (KLB). Authorities emphasize the need for laboratory confirmation to determine outbreak status. In response, the Health Office is implementing catch-up immunization (immunization kejar) for children who missed vaccines and intensifying Vitamin A supplementation for vulnerable groups, especially infants and toddlers. No infection source is identified, and there is no mention of imported or exported cases.",
        "articleId": "aHR0cHM6Ly9rYWx0aW0udHJpYnVubmV3cy5jb20vdHJpYnVuLWV0YW0vMTE0MDgwMy9iZWx1bS1zdGF0dXMta2xiLWRpbmtlcy1zYW1hcmluZGEtcGFzdGlrYW4tNzIta2FzdXMtYmFydS1zZWJhdGFzLXN1c3Blay1tZWRpcw=="
