        "articleSummary": "In Kolkata, doctors link severe COVID-19 forms to genetic immune defects (Inborn Errors of Immunity). At the first East India conference on Inborn Errors of Immunity, Dr. Priyankar Pal and Dr. Jigna Vattiya said congenital immune defects can predispose individuals to dangerous COVID-19 outcomes, with some producing antibodies that undermine protective immune proteins. The Indian Society for Primary Immunodeficiency Disorders and an international body (IAPID) organized the event. They noted that IEIs are often diagnosed in newborns, presenting as frequent infections with only temporary relief from antibiotics. In Kolkata's Institute of Child Health, a five-year-old Bihar resident admitted with TB-like symptoms was diagnosed with Chronic Granulomatous Disease (CGD) after identifying Nocardia bacteria; no tuberculosis. Diagnostic tests highlighted elevated neutrophil counts or CRP, plus lymphocyte-subset analysis and genetic testing as key tools.",
        "articleId": "aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc2FuZ2JhZHByYXRpZGluLmluL2xpZmVzdHlsZS9oZWFsdGgvY292aWQtd2FzLW9jY3VycmVkLWR1ZS10by1nZW5ldGljcy1wcm9ibGVtL3BpZC8xMTQ1NDA5Lw=="
