        "articleSummary": "An HIV-positive man in Hyderabad’s Pocharam ITI Police Station area lured a 22-year-old woman to his home after her family refused to approve the marriage. Following the woman's HIV-positive result, the suspect—also HIV-positive—allegedly injected his own blood into her body on March 11, resulting in the woman contracting HIV. Police filed a case of attempt to murder and arrested him; the woman is hospitalized. Investigators are examining whether others were involved. The incident is linked to the groom’s and his parents’ HIV status influencing the marriage decision. The case highlights risks of intimate-partner transmission and the use of infected blood as a weapon; authorities continue the probe.",
