        "articleSummary": "Six years after the first Covid-19 case in Bahia, Brazil, COVID-19 deaths persist. Sesab reports five COVID-19–associated deaths in 2026. In early 2026, Bahia recorded 919 Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome (SRAG) cases, with 32 deaths; of these, five were due to COVID-19 and one to influenza; remaining deaths under investigation or attributed to other respiratory viruses. The data show continued circulation of both SARS-CoV-2 and influenza, though not at pandemic or emergency levels, with hospitalizations occurring. Vaccination remains key to reducing severe outcomes; keep immunizations up to date. Higher hospitalization risk for SRAG among children; deaths concentrated among elderly. The first Bahia COVID-19 death occurred 29 March 2020, a 74-year-old man in Salvador. Authorities emphasize vigilance and basic prevention, particularly for vulnerable groups.",
