        "articleSummary": "As of the ninth week of 2026, Berau Health Office reports 42 suspected measles cases, with all cases still classified as suspects pending laboratory confirmation. Samples from Berau are routed first to the provincial level, then to the Balai Besar Teknik Kesehatan Lingkungan dan Pengendalian Penyakit (BBTKLPP) in Banjarbaru; if Banjarbaru is at capacity, specimens may be sent to Jakarta. Laboratory results can take up to two months. Despite awaiting lab confirmation, case management is initiated immediately based on doctors' diagnoses and medical teams' assessments to prevent deterioration. Most suspected cases are in Sambaliung District, and more than 80% involve individuals who were not vaccinated against measles, which is preventable by immunization (PD3I). Unvaccinated patients tend to present more severe symptoms and have higher risks of complications or death; measles mostly affects children, especially infants and toddlers, though adults can be affected.",
