        "articleSummary": "Santa Bárbara d'Oeste's Vigilance Department of Zoonoses reports intensified Aedes aegypti control to prevent dengue, Zika, and chikungunya. From January to March 11, 2026, 5,708 blocking-and-breeding-site visits were conducted across neighborhoods including Santa Rosa II, Jardim Pérola, Cidade Nova, Planalto do Sol, Parque Zabani, Conjunto dos Trabalhadores, Terras de São Pedro, 31 de Março, Jardim Batagin, Vila Grego, Residencial Furlan, Jardim Conceição, Jardim São Francisco, Jardim Santa Alice, Vista Alegre, Chácaras Beira Rio, and Cruzeiro do Sul. They found 6,987 water containers, with 263 containing Ae. aegypti larvae. Additional vector-control activities included 44,519 home visits, 2,710 portable nebulizations, 1,580 ovitrampas surveyed, and 3,097 maintenance actions on larvicidal stations, plus 5,890 vehicular biolarvicide applications. Community involvement is essential; residents should host health agents, seal and cover water storage, clean gutters and pools, and install screens. Suspected dengue symptoms warrant local health care at (19) 3463-8099.",
