        "articleSummary": "Phuket, Thailand — 13 Russian guests at MBC Condotel were diagnosed with conjunctivitis and a gastrointestinal infection, with symptoms beginning in late February. Patients reported eye inflammation, vomiting/diarrhea, and high fever; symptoms align with rotavirus infection. Illness linked to tap water described as foul-smelling and turbid, with illness attributed to water exposure. Earlier in February, 19 Russians at the same hotel reported nausea and abdominal pains, suggesting a broader outbreak at the property. Diarrhea and vomiting have affected guests and other hotels, including foreigners; pharmacies reported heavy demand for medicines. No laboratory confirmation is cited in the report, and the article does not specify investigations or official findings. As of 2026-03-15, the situation involves a water-associated outbreak at a Phuket hotel with gastrointestinal illness and conjunctivitis.\"}{",
