        "articleSummary": "About 35% of Haryana's gram panchayats are eligible for TB-free certification in 2025 under the TB Mukt Panchayat initiative. The effort aims to eliminate tuberculosis through a tiered TB-free certification system, launched by Prime Minister Narendra Modi on World Tuberculosis Day, March 24, 2023, in Varanasi. Sumita Misra, Additional Chief Secretary of the Haryana health department, confirmed the milestone, highlighting grassroots momentum. In 2023, Haryana awarded 574 bronze TB-free certifications; in 2024, certifications rose to 1,855, including silver levels. By 2025, 2,157 panchayats were eligible for certification, underscoring active local governance engagement in the TB elimination mission. The tiered system seeks to sustain TB-free status and strengthen locally delivered TB prevention, early detection, and treatment through community accountability and healthy rivalry among panchayats.",
