        "articleSummary": "First detection of avian influenza in wild birds reported in late February at the Taim Ecological Reserve, Rio Grande do Sul. By March 12, 2026, 23 birds—coscoroba swans and garça-moura (a type of heron)—were collected with the disease. The DDA/Seapi trained 186 health and social-service agents and held meetings with municipal managers in Rio Grande, Santa Vitória do Palmar, and Chuí to align prevention and control. Aimed at surveillance and containment, authorities conducted a sanitary sweep around the outbreak, inspecting 93 subsistence poultry properties within 10 km, plus commercial farms in the Pelotas area and ornament bird breeders in Santa Vitória do Palmar. In integrated action with ICMBio and Mapa, SVO-RS monitors Lagoa da Mangueira, collecting samples sent to LFDA-SP (OMSA reference) for confirmation. Suspect cases (respiratory or neurological signs, high mortality) should be reported via Inspetorias or e-Sisbravet or WhatsApp (51) 98445-2033.",
        "articleId": "aHR0cHM6Ly9zb3VhZ3JvLm5ldC9ub3RpY2lhLzIwMjYvMDMvZXN0YWRvLXNlZ3VlLWNvbS1hY29lcy1kZS1tb25pdG9yYW1lbnRvLWEtZ3JpcGUtYXZpYXJpYS8="
      },
