        "articleSummary": "Six measles cases detected among children under 10 in Pati Regency, Indonesia, with four cases in Tayu District and one each in Tambakromo and Sukolilo, as of March 2026. Data from Dinkes Kabupaten Pati indicate infections likely among unvaccinated youngsters. Classic symptoms include high fever 38–40°C, persistent cough, runny nose, red eyes, fatigue, and loss of appetite, followed by a rash that begins behind the ears and face and spreads to the neck, body, arms, and legs. Koplik spots in the mouth are highlighted as a hallmark. Health officials anticipate ongoing transmission and plan to intensify vaccination campaigns to curb spread. No laboratory confirmation details beyond health office data; no fatalities reported in the article. Emphasizes vaccination to prevent further outbreaks in the district and province.",
