        "articleSummary": "Foot-and-Mouth Disease (FMD) vaccination drive launched statewide in Andhra Pradesh for cattle and buffaloes from March 16 to April 29 under the National Animal Disease Control Programme. The free, door-to-door campaign will cover all animals over four months of age, in two phases: March 16–April 14 and April 15–29 to administer booster doses. Officials have distributed 8.37 million vaccine doses across districts. FMD is a highly contagious viral disease threatening livestock and farmers’ livelihoods; cross-bred cattle are especially susceptible, while indigenous breeds fare better. Infected animals may show high fever, mouth and hoof blisters, udder swelling, excessive salivation, and difficulty walking; calves face higher death risk, milk production declines, and pregnant animals may abort. Vaccination aims to avert economic losses, with Director of Animal Husbandry T. Damodar Naidu urging farmers to cooperate.",
