        "articleSummary": "A 1-year-11-month-old Yanomami girl from the Xitei community in the Yanomami Indigenous Territory (spanning Amazonas and Roraima) died on Saturday while being airlifted to Boa Vista. The infant, who weighed 6.1 kg, suffered severe malnutrition, malaria, and intestinal parasitosis (ascariasis) and developed respiratory failure with Loeffler syndrome during the flight, with dehydration signs noted. The evacuation was requested around 10:29 and occurred about six hours later, around 16:20; she died around 17:30 as the aircraft approached Boa Vista. The body was returned to the community on Sunday. Health authorities (Dsei-Y and the Ministry of Health) monitor the case amid a broader Yanomami health emergency since January 2023, with indigenous leaders blaming delays and resource gaps in delivering care inside the territory, amid reports of ongoing illegal mining and prior child deaths.",
