        "articleSummary": "Chickenpox remains active in Ernakulam district, Kerala, with over 900 cases reported since January 2026. Across Kerala, 1,897 cases were recorded in March 2026 alone, bringing the year-to-date total to 11,388. Three deaths statewide this year. Doctors say no surge, but cases align with the summer season. Transmission is airborne and can occur even before vesicles appear; patients with fever should isolate and seek medical care promptly. Lesions typically begin on the trunk (torso, chest, stomach, back) and can be numerous, itchy, with fever and body aches. Vulnerable groups—adolescents, adults, and those with low immunity such as cancer or diabetes patients—are at higher risk of complications. Vaccination is advised for at-risk individuals to prevent severe disease; clinicians emphasize early care and public vigilance.",
