        "articleSummary": "Andhra Pradesh launches statewide free vaccination drive against Foot-and-Mouth Disease for cattle and buffaloes, including calves over four months, under the National Animal Disease Control Programme. Campaign runs March 16–April 29, 2026, in two phases: main round March 16–April 14 and second phase April 15–29, with vaccines administered at owners' homes free of charge. State has supplied 83.69 lakh vaccine doses to districts for the campaign. FMD is a highly contagious viral disease affecting cattle and buffaloes; cross-bred animals are more vulnerable. Vaccination is described as the only effective preventive measure. Transmission occurs via wounds, contaminated fodder, feed, water, dung, and urine of infected animals. Symptoms include fever 104-106°F, mouth and lip blisters, excessive salivation, hoof and udder blisters causing lameness. Calves may die after consuming milk; pregnant animals may abort; recovery can take up to six months. Economic losses loom due to milk decline and reduced work capacity.",
