        "articleSummary": "Intersectoral mobilization in Cuiabá, Brazil, targets Aedes aegypti breeding sites to prevent dengue, Zika, and chikungunya. The city’s SMS-led task force plans to cover 53 neighborhoods and about 83,836 properties, with ~285 Endemic Disease Control Agents and support from Community Health Agents. Initiated on February 24, 2026, and running through May 5, 2026 (39 days), the campaign operates four days per week, weather permitting. To date, eight neighborhoods have been served, reaching ~13,237 residents with guidance, property inspections, and removal of standing-water sources. Early areas: Planalto, Novo Terceiro, Coophamil, 1º de Março, Parque Atalaia, Bela Vista, Cidade Alta, José Pinto. The “Ação Única” strategy combines ACEs and ACSs in a single visit to address all sanitation needs. Remaining neighborhoods include Três Barras, Jardim Liberdade, Novo Colorado, among others. After neighborhood completion, Primary Health assumes ongoing family and property monitoring to prevent reintroduction; public participation is essential.",
