        "articleSummary": "Cholera remains active in Kinshasa, Democratic Republic of Congo, but conditions are improving after authorities’ measures. In Kinshasa province, about 240 new suspected cholera cases and deaths were reported; 84 active patients are treated in cholera centers, up from 41 a week earlier. At Makala Central Prison, six active cholera cases are hospitalized; total recoveries reach 187 and five deaths have been recorded since Feb 12, 2026. The INRB confirmed 13 positive cases from 17 samples; among confirmed, four recovered and five deaths. Fifteen new suspected cases were identified on Feb 13, 2026. A Feb 14 circular by Justice Minister Guillaume Ngefa Atondoko Andali bans new admissions to Makala, tightens visits, and orders strengthened sanitation, medicines, disinfection, and daily epidemiological reporting in coordination with the Health Ministry. Mpox: in week 9, suspected cases rose from 258 to 285; since 2024, 123,762 suspected and 34,822 confirmed.",
