        "articleSummary": "In early 2026, Cuiabá recorded 323 dengue notifications with 139 confirmed, a 79.2% decrease from the same period in 2025. Chikungunya showed 59 notifications with 58 confirmed, down 99.3% in Q1, while Zika had 4 notifications with no confirmed cases. The reductions follow intensified Aedes aegypti control efforts across the city. From January to March 2026, 197,192 properties were inspected by Endemic Combat Agents; 21,672 required direct treatment, 24,344 water-containing deposits were treated, and 6,559 mosquito breeding sites were eliminated. Prevention guidance emphasizes removing standing water from containers, sealing water tanks, cleaning gutters and drains, using repellents as directed, and allowing endemic-control agents access for inspections. The measures target multiple Cuiabá neighborhoods to curb transmission of dengue, chikungunya, and Zika.",
