        "articleSummary": "Measles in São Paulo marks Brazil's first case in 2026. A 6-month-old girl, unvaccinated and resident of São Paulo, contracted measles after exposure linked to Bolivia, where an outbreak has been ongoing since 2025. The child traveled to Bolivia from 25 December 2025 to 25 January 2026; the case is considered imported. Laboratory confirmation occurred in early March 2026 by the São Paulo municipality after genomic sequencing, with the Ministry of Health noting the import origin. This is the first confirmed measles case in the State of São Paulo in 2026; São Paulo state had two imported cases in 2025. Nationwide, Brazil reported 38 confirmed cases in 2025 (Tocantins 25; Mato Grosso 6; Rio de Janeiro 2; São Paulo 2; Distrito Federal 1; Rio Grande do Sul 1; Maranhão 1). Bolivia has an ongoing outbreak near Brazil’s borders with Mato Grosso do Sul and Tocantins. Measles is highly contagious; vaccination is crucial; symptoms include fever, red rash, cough, conjunctivitis; complications include pneumonia, encephalitis, dehydration; transmission is airborne.",
