        "articleSummary": "Measles cases surged at the start of 2026, with 45 outbreaks reported across 29 districts/cities in 11 provinces as of week 8. Week 7 recorded 9,947 suspected cases and 7,922 confirmed cases with 5 deaths; week 8 rose to 10,453 suspected and 8,372 confirmed cases, with 6 deaths. In response, the Ministry of Health accelerated immunization, targeting 102 districts/cities for outbreak response immunization aimed at children aged 9–59 months. The program concentrates on outbreak-affected areas through Outbreak Response Immunization and on high-risk regions via a Catch-Up Campaign to immunize those not yet reached. The surge signals ongoing measles transmission early in 2026, prompting intensified vaccination to curb spread across the affected provinces. Keywords: vaccination, outbreak response, catch-up campaign, measles, public health.",
