        "articleSummary": "New reassortant lineage of Oropouche virus circulating in Southeast Brazil, with 55 confirmed infections in Rio de Janeiro and Minas Gerais from December 2024 to May 2025. Researchers from Universidade Federal Fluminense analyzed 55 confirmed cases; genetic sequencing identifies a reassortant lineage, indicating genome segment reorganization and adaptation to the Southeast, suggesting potential longer-term establishment with variable circulation. Findings published January 7 in Open Forum Infectious Diseases. Clinically, most patients reported severe headaches and malaise (87%), along with fever, myalgia, and skin rashes. This expands the virus’s geographic range beyond its historic Amazon region association. No deaths reported in the study; authors warn of ongoing regional circulation and possible shifts in epidemiology.",
