        "articleSummary": "Hepatitis A cases rise in Ribeirão Preto, São Paulo, Brazil, prompting a health alert. From January through March 2026, the city recorded 203 Hepatitis A cases, compared with only 2 in the same period of 2025. Officials say the increase began in December and has persisted, described as a surge beyond what is expected but not exponential. Transmission occurs via contaminated water, food or objects, and through close contact or sharing utensils; sexual transmission with fecal-oral exposure is possible. No single contamination point has been identified; authorities investigate case-by-case and coordinate with healthcare networks to provide laboratory diagnostics. Symptoms typically begin with fatigue, fever and nausea, followed by gastrointestinal symptoms; darker urine and jaundice can appear in advanced stages. Vaccination against Hepatitis A is available through the SUS in all city vaccination sites and is advised for children and at-risk groups. Prevention emphasizes hygiene and vaccination; avoid alcohol during treatment.",
