        "articleSummary": "Araçatuba, Brazil, launches a new phase of dengue vector control focused on Aedes aegypti, which transmits dengue, chikungunya, and Zika. Starting Monday, March 16, through Wednesday, March 18, operations run from 6:30 PM in the neighborhoods of São Vicente, Novo Paraíso, Paraíso, and Jardim Brasil. A vehicle-mounted fogging system (Nebulização Acoplada a Veículo, NAV) disperses insecticide to target adult mosquitoes in street and residential areas. The initiative follows intensified house-to-house visits by municipal health agents and the removal of potential breeding containers, with reinforced resident guidance on preventive measures. The effort is conducted with the support of the Coordinadoria de Controle de Doenças, under the Secretaria de Estado da Saúde. The article does not provide case counts or laboratory confirmation.",
