        "articleSummary": "Measles cases in Indonesia declined from 531 to 511 weekly cases by week nine of 2026, according to the Ministry of Health in Jakarta. The drop follows intensified immunization and widespread hygiene education across several regions, with Outbreak Response Immunization (ORI) and catch-up campaigns in districts experiencing outbreaks or rising cases. Acting Director General of Disease Control Andi Saguni warns that measles is highly infectious, with one case potentially spreading to 12–18 others, mainly among young children, though adults are occasionally affected. Immunization relies on two doses at 9 and 18 months: first-dose coverage is about 80%, rising to 97% after the second dose. The program aims to sustain reductions nationwide through continued vaccination and public health messaging.",
