        ],
        "articleSummary": "Measles outbreaks in Indonesia continued through Week 9, 2026, with 8,716 reported cases and 10,826 suspected, rising by about 500 cases in Week 9. By March 12, 2026, 45 outbreaks (KLB) were recorded across 29 districts in 11 provinces, including North Sumatra, West Sumatra, South Sumatra, Banten, West Java, Central Java, Yogyakarta, East Java, NTB, South Sulawesi, and Central Sulawesi, though weekly lab-confirmed trends were generally down, except in NTB (Bima and Kota Bima) remaining high. The top districts for suspected/case load include Tangerang Selatan, Bima, Tangerang, Depok, Jakarta Pusat, Palembang, and Padang. Outbreak Response Immunization (ORI MR) targeting ages 9–59 months was underway in 22 districts/cities, with highest coverage in Pamekasan 47.93%, Jember 38.64%, and Bima 22.73%. Catch-Up MR immunization (CuC) showed Jakarta Pusat 80.4%, Jakarta Barat 56.4%, Depok 17.3%, Tangerang Selatan 8.4%, Palu 5.6%. Fifty-one health offices coordinate MR rollout; parents are urged to verify 9- and 18-month immunizations and seek care for fever, rash, cough, or red eyes to reduce transmission. Measles remains highly contagious (one case can infect 12–18 others).",
        "articleId": "aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYW50YXJhbmV3cy5jb20vYmVyaXRhLzU0NzQ2OTgvODcxNi1rYXN1cy1jYW1wYWstcGVyLW1pbmdndS1rZS05LWtlbWVua2VzLWdlbmNhcmthbi1pbXVuaXNhc2k="
