        "articleSummary": "Measles outbreak in Padang, West Sumatra: Puskesmas Andalas Padang recorded 105 residents suspected of measles infection in 2025, prompting a mass Outbreak Response Immunization (ORI) campaign in the affected area. The public health response aims to curb transmission in Padang’s Andalas district. Separately, a high-profile incident in Padang involved a 50-year-old housewife (AY) burned by her adopted son, after being doused with Pertalite fuel, on March 12, 2026 at a bus terminal Loket AKAP on Jalan Prof. Dr. Hamka, Air Tawar Barat, Padang Utara. Ombudsman Sumbar also oversaw Lebaran mudik preparations at Terminal Anak Air Padang and Minangkabau International Airport; facilities were complete, but only 4 of 9 AKAP operators were active at Terminal Anak Air. Collectively, these reports reflect health and safety issues in Padang, West Sumatra, as of March 14, 2026.",
