        "articleSummary": "Measles outbreak (KLB) declared in 11 Indonesian provinces including West Java, with Depok highlighted for intensified immunization. As of week 9 in 2026, Indonesia reported 8,716 laboratory-confirmed measles cases nationwide, with about 500 new cases that week. Week 8 saw 10,453 suspected cases, 8,372 confirmed, and 6 deaths; week 7 had 8,224 suspected, 572 confirmed, and 4 deaths. A total of 45 KLB outbreaks across 29 districts/cities in 11 provinces (North Sumatra, West Sumatra, South Sumatra, Banten, West Java, Central Java, Yogyakarta, East Java, West Nusa Tenggara, South and Central Sulawesi) are listed, with most weekly trends declining except NTB (Bima regency and City) remaining high. Top districts by suspected/cases include Tangerang Selatan, Bima, Tangerang, Depok, Central Jakarta, Palembang, and Padang. By March 12, 2026, 22 districts/cities conducted Outbreak Response Immunization (ORI MR) for ages 9–59 months; highest ORI MR coverage in Pamekasan 47.93%, Jember 38.64%, Bima 22.73%. For Catch-Up Immunization MR (CuC), Jakarta Barat 56.4%, Jakarta Pusat 80.4%, Depok 17.3%, Tangerang Selatan 8.4%, Palu 5.6%. Fifty-one UPT Kekarantinaan Kesehatan support MR immunization, coordinating with local health offices. Parents should verify measles vaccination status at 9 and 18 months, monitor fever, rash, cough, runny nose, and red eyes, seek care if symptoms appear, and avoid travel to prevent transmission, given measles’ high contagiousness (one case can infect 12–18 people).",
