        "articleSummary": "Jakarta's health authorities are urged to heighten measles vigilance ahead of Lebaran as mobility and family gatherings rise. Measles is highly contagious, spreading via droplets when people cough or sneeze or through close contact. Commission E DPRD Secretary Justin Adrian Untayana called on the DKI Jakarta provincial government to follow Health Ministry guidance with proactive measures, especially for children not fully immunized. Authorities should maintain high coverage of measles and MR (Measles-Rubella) vaccination, and optimize primary care facilities—puskesmas and posyandu—to verify immunization status and prevent missed children. Surveillance and rapid response for suspected measles cases must be reinforced to curb potential spread. No specific case counts are provided; the emphasis is on preparedness for potential outbreaks during increased travel around Eid.",
