        "articleSummary": "TB patients may undertake Lebaran mudik; there is no prohibition, but precautions apply. Pulmonologist Dr. Herman, Sp.P, FISR, told Health Liputan6.com in Bogor that TB patients should wear masks when traveling, especially during the first two weeks when infectiousness is highest. After two weeks, transmission risk declines, yet masking is advised when meeting crowds; if the patient remains negative after two months, a sputum test should be repeated. If sputum is negative, the patient is no longer contagious and can resume normal activities without masks. He notes ongoing measles outbreaks context; TB is bacterial, measles viral. If a TB patient contracts measles, both conditions require treatment—TB with anti-TB drugs, measles with antiviral therapy—taken at different times to avoid stomach upset. Location: Bogor, RS EMC Sentul. Date: 14 March 2026.",
