        "articleHeadlineTranslated": "Corrections explains that Amp Nawat, a detainee in a Section 112 case, is not ill with monkeypox or chickenpox.",
        "articleBody": "",
        "affectedCategories": [
          {
            "id": 1,
            "name": "humans"
          }
        ],
        "articleSummary": "Bangkok Remand Prison clarified on 14 March 2026 that detainee Nawat Liengwatthana, aka ‘Amp,’ a Section 112 defendant, is not ill with monkeypox or chickenpox. Detained since 2 July 2024, he was found on 7 March 2026 to have one inflamed wound on the left ankle and two red bumps on the right thigh, with mild local pain and no fever, prompting isolated observation. On 10 March 2026, prior to a court appearance, an on-duty physician concluded there was no evidence of monkeypox or chickenpox, allowing release from quarantine. On 11 March 2026, nurses re-evaluated, explained the condition, and continued daily wound care and medications at the prison hospital. The detainee understood the diagnosis, showed no anxiety, and monitoring continues by prison medical staff. ",
        "articleId": "aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmFld25hLmNvbS9sb2NhbC85NTI2NjU="
      },
