        "articleSummary": "An abandoned house at Rua José Geraldo de Castro Paes 221 in Pau Amarelo, Paulista, within the Recife metropolitan area, is identified as a focal point for dengue-carrying mosquitoes, raising health concerns for nearby residents. Residents report a proliferation of dengue vectors at the property, with illnesses affecting the elderly and children in the surrounding neighborhood. The letter requests the Paulista City Health Secretariat and the Sanitation Surveillance agency to take immediate measures to eliminate breeding sites. It underscores ongoing dengue risk in the Greater Recife region and the need for vector control, property cleanup, and community engagement. No laboratory confirmation or case counts are provided. Other letters touch on unrelated issues (public transport shelters, sewage odor, travel), but the dengue situation is highlighted as a potential outbreak driver.",
