        "articleSummary": "Rabies case in Mirzapur district, Uttar Pradesh, India: 17-year-old Karn, a class 8 student from Jogi Purwa village in the Kachhwa area, bitten by a dog four months earlier. Family administered only two injections of the post-exposure vaccination course, neglecting the full five-dose schedule. The virus has since invaded his nervous system, producing rapid behavioral changes: voice turning into a canine bark, walking on all fours, and altered posture. He is now in the final stage of rabies, with hydrophobia noted by doctors; treatment is deemed futile and survival unlikely. Medical college physicians warn that incomplete vaccination after dog bites invites fatal infection. He has been placed in quarantine as doctors emphasize the necessity of completing the full five-dose vaccination regimen after any dog bite. The report serves as a stark caution against underestimating dog bites.",
