        "articleSummary": "Measles cases in Indonesia have begun to decline, according to the Ministry of Health. In week 9, new measles cases fell to 231, down from 511 the previous week. Totals up to week 9 include 10,829 suspected cases and 8,716 laboratory-confirmed measles cases, with 45 extraordinary outbreak events (KLB) reported across 29 districts/cities in 11 provinces. The briefing, held at the Health Ministry in South Jakarta on March 13, 2026, attributed the downturn to rapid immunization responses in KLB-affected areas. Immunization activities—Outbreak Response Immunization (ORI)—were implemented across all districts with outbreaks, while non-KLB areas saw catch-up campaigns to accelerate measles vaccination. The data reflect ongoing outbreaks but show a weekly decrease, underscoring the impact of intensified vaccination efforts in Indonesia.",
