        "articleSummary": "Dengue fever remains a public threat in Vietnam, with 168,140 cases and 33 deaths from early 2025 to date. During the 9‑day Tet holiday, 1,431 cases were recorded; since 2026 began, four dengue deaths have occurred. On 12 March, the Ministry of Health warned rising case numbers in the South, Central Highlands, and northern cities such as Hanoi, Hai Phong, and Quang Ninh. Ho Chi Minh City has reported over 11,621 dengue cases this year. With hot, humid, and rainy conditions, peaks are forecast: June in the South/Central regions; August–November in the North. The MOH 2026 plan emphasizes intersectoral coordination and local four-on-site measures, surveillance, vaccination, and treatment. Qdenga vaccine is available for people aged 4+, reducing infection risk by over 80% and hospitalization risk by over 90%. Transmission is via Aedes mosquitoes. Preventive actions include eliminating standing water, protective clothing, repellents; if infected, rest, fluids, and paracetamol; avoid NSAIDs.",
