        "articleSummary": "Measles alert in Klaten Regency, Central Java, as the Klaten Health Office warns of ongoing transmission and outlines symptoms and prevention. The disease is caused by the measles virus (rubeola, a paramyxovirus) and spreads mainly via respiratory droplets from coughing or sneezing; casual physical contact is less likely to transmit. Symptoms to watch include red blotches on the skin, red eyes, mild fever, and cough, with rash described as red macules rather than bumps or crusts. Health official Anggit Budiarto emphasizes that measles is highly contagious and serious if not addressed early. Prevention focuses on PHBS (Clean and Healthy Living Behavior), regular handwashing with soap, and ensuring nutritious meals for children under five to boost immunity. The report does not provide case counts, laboratory confirmation, or infection sources, and highlights public guidance on reducing gatherings when unwell.",
