        "articleSummary": "Vietnam's livestock sector faces hidden diseases and challenges in antibiotic use control and product traceability, issues to be addressed at the National Conference on Livestock Science and Veterinary Medicine 2026, March 27–28, hosted by the Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development. The event will review research and development outcomes for 2021–2025 and set priorities for 2026–2030, aiming to strengthen the 'three-way' linkage among regulators, scientists, and industry to advance sustainable, safe, and environmentally friendly livestock production, disease control, food safety, and biosecurity. Topics include animal breeding, biotechnology, nutrition, vaccines, and disease management. The report also highlights intensified Nipah virus surveillance at pig farms, particularly in areas with high density of fruit bats, calling for active monitoring of pigs with respiratory or neurological signs to prevent spillover and protect livelihoods.",
