        "articleSummary": "Three deaths from chikungunya were reported in the Dourados Indigenous Reserve, about 233 km from Campo Grande, Mato Grosso do Sul, per SES epidemiological bulletin. The most recent death is a 3-month-old baby who developed symptoms March 6 and died March 10; lab confirmation came March 11 via Lacen. A 73-year-old man without comorbidities developed symptoms February 4 and died February 9. Earlier, a 69-year-old woman from Jaguapiru village developed symptoms February 13 and died February 25 due to chikungunya complications; she had hypertension and diabetes. Dourados records 386 suspected and 206 confirmed cases; data are not broken down by district. Fatima do Sul reports 460 notifications and 453 confirmed. In Dourados, at least half of cases involve pregnant women (five in the second trimester and two in the third); statewide, 16 pregnant women have chikungunya.",
