        "articleSummary": "On 14 March 2026, Kalemie in Tanganyika province launched a mass free distribution campaign of preventive chemotherapy medicines against neglected tropical diseases in Kalemie commune. Initiated by Benoît Malumbi Muhiya, Tanganyika's provincial health minister, the drive targets all residents aged five and above to reduce morbidity from onchocerciasis, trachoma, lymphatic filariasis, schistosomiasis, and geohelminthiases (soil-transmitted helminths). Success depends on broad adherence and active participation of health actors and partners, with funding from technical and financial partners, according to Ruth Luabeya. Pierrot Bolunza, provincial health division chief, underscored the need for strong community engagement. The campaign aims to relieve the population from the burden of neglected tropical diseases through free medicines distributed within Kalemie, supported by international partners.",
