        "articleSummary": "DOH reported 486 new HIV diagnoses in the Philippines during Oct–Dec 2025 among individuals involved in transactional sex, per the October–December 2025 HIV Surveillance of the Philippines. Transactional sex is defined as having either paid for sex, been paid for sex, or both in the past 12 months. Breakdown: 235 cases among men who paid for sex; 171 cases among those who received payment for sex (162 men, 9 women). Additionally, 80 people living with HIV (PLHIV) reported both paying and receiving payment for sex (77 men, 3 women). Since reporting began in December 2012, total HIV cases in this group reach 18,275. Indicates ongoing transmission linked to transactional sex across the country, underscoring continued public-health focus on this risk factor in the Philippines.",
        "articleId": "aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuc3Vuc3Rhci5jb20ucGgvc3VwZXJiYWxpdGEtY2VidS9kdWwtYW4tc2EtNTAwLW5hdGFwdGFuLXNhLWhpdi1ndW1pa2Fuc2EtcHJvdGl0dXN5b24="
