        "articleSummary": "Dengue outbreak in Santarém, western Pará, Brazil, with a public health emergency declared after a surge in cases. As of 14 March 2026, 1,409 dengue cases were notified, 276 of which are laboratory-confirmed; six dengue-related deaths have been confirmed, with one death under investigation. The mayor signed the emergency decree on 13 March 2026 to enable rapid actions, including intensifying vector-control efforts, expanding field teams to eliminate mosquito breeding sites, conducting neighborhood mutirões (cleanup drives) in high-incidence areas, strengthening epidemiological surveillance, and expanding health-care capacity across units. Authorities urge residents to eliminate standing water, keep yards clean, seal water tanks, discard containers that collect water, and report potential mosquito breeding sites. Health and environmental surveillance teams are mobilized citywide to bolster prevention and control of transmission.",
