        "articleSummary": "In India, a 24-year-old man allegedly injected HIV-infected blood into a woman after a marriage arrangement between relatives was abandoned due to his HIV-positive status. The act occurred on March 11, following an initial family agreement; the engagement was canceled when tests revealed the man’s HIV positivity, prompting the woman’s parents to retract. Police arrested him on charges of attempted murder. The victim is hospitalized as investigations continue. The case highlights the severe risk of intentional exposure to HIV in the context of rejected matrimonial plans, with authorities examining the circumstances surrounding the act and ongoing investigations into the incident.",
