        "articleSummary": "Rabies case reported in Mirzapur district, Uttar Pradesh, India: a 14-year-old boy named Karan developed rabies symptoms about four months after being bitten by a stray dog at the end of the previous year. He presented hydrophobia (fear of water) and dog-like vocalizations, leading to admission at Kachhwa Health Center. Rabies was confirmed after examination. The case highlights the incubation variability of the rabies virus, which travels via nerves to the brain; incubation can span weeks to months depending on bite site and viral load. The infection source was a stray dog bite, and the family’s failure to administer timely anti-rabies vaccination contributed to the risk. This is a single reported case illustrating delayed onset and the importance of seeking care after exposure to potentially rabid animals.",
