        "articleSummary": "AIIMS expanded from 6 to 23 institutes, strengthening tertiary care and medical education across India. Maternal Mortality Ratio declined by about 86%, far above the global ~48% reduction. TB incidence fell by 21%, outperforming the global 12% decline per WHO. Out-of-pocket health expenditure dropped from 62.6% to 39.4%, reducing financial burden on citizens. The Lancet reports about 90% of cancer patients in India begin treatment within 20 days, indicating improved diagnosis and care pathways. Ayushman Bharat Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (PM-JAY) is described as the world’s largest health coverage scheme, offering up to Rs 5 lakh per family for secondary and tertiary hospitalization and benefiting over 71 crore people. These gains were highlighted by Union Health Minister J.P. Nadda at Teerthanker Mahaveer University’s convocation in Moradabad, urging graduates to contribute to society with social responsibility.",
