        "articleSummary": "As of March 14, 2026, West Java health authorities warn of measles transmission during Lebaran 2026 homecoming. Measles spreads easily via coughing or sneezing droplets, direct contact with an infected person, or touching contaminated objects, according to Raden Vini Adiani Dewi, Head of the West Java Health Office, speaking in Bandung. A single case can infect 12–18 people. January–February 2026 saw 252 measles cases in West Java; 2025 total reached 1,785, up from 271 the year before. The most effective preventive measure is completing the measles immunization up to the second dose before Mudik (Idul Fitri homecoming), particularly for children aged 9–59 months. Authorities emphasize vaccination campaigns and public awareness ahead of mass travel to limit transmission.",
