        "articleSummary": "As of March 14, 2026, Vigilância Ambiental em Saúde (VAS) in Botucatu, Brazil confirmed a bat (Myotis nigricans) found in Vila São Lúcio tested positive for rabies, with laboratory confirmation. Bats are common in urban areas and can act as reservoirs for the rabies virus; no human cases are reported in this note. Do not handle a fallen or debilitated bat; isolate it, keep dogs and cats away, and contact VAS at (14) 3811-1609 for safe rescue. Antirabies vaccine doses are currently prioritized for animals with exposure; routine vaccination of dogs and cats will resume once vaccine distribution to municipalities is regularized. Background: Brazil hosts ~180 bat species, with 41 identified in the Botucatu region. For after-hours bat rescue, call 153 (Guarda Civil Municipal).",
