        "articleSummary": "Americana hosted the Capacitation in Clinical Management of Arboviral Diseases on March 13, 2026, organized by the GVE Campinas with Americana’s Epidemiological Surveillance and the Municipal Health Secretariat. At the Faculdade de Americana, 147 health professionals from Americana and neighboring cities (Santa Bárbara d'Oeste, Campinas, Cosmópolis) were trained. Infectious disease physician Dr. Alessa de Andrade Santana (Unicamp) updated attendees on evidence-based management of arboviruses within SUS, aiming to standardize clinical workflows and strengthen regional integration. The event was reinforced by the Health Secretary Danilo Carvalho Oliveira, who underscored ongoing training to improve early case recognition and treatment. Arboviruses, transmitted by arthropods such as Aedes aegypti, include dengue, Zika and chikungunya. Parallel actions by PMCD operate mutirões to remove breeding sites in São Jerônimo; initiatives include ADL surveys, site inspections, AI-based geomonitoring, and a public campaign 'A dengue não vai ter vez em 2026.' Dengue cases have fallen, but prevention continues.",
