        "articleSummary": "Chikungunya fever in Mato Grosso do Sul, Brazil, reached a decade-high mortality in 2026, with Dourados as epicenter. By epidemiological week 09 (through Mar 7), 3 confirmed deaths and 1,147 confirmed cases in the state, including 16 pregnant women. All three fatalities occurred in Dourados: a 73-year-old man (symptoms Feb 4; death about a month later; no comorbidity), a 69-year-old woman with hypertension and diabetes (symptoms Feb 13; death ~12 days later), and a 3-month-old infant (symptoms Mar 6; death four days after). Since 2015, MS has logged 7,143 probable cases through 2024; 2025 saw a surge with 2,122 probable by early March, and 2026 is tracking toward similar levels (2,446 probable so far). Historically, 2023 had 3 deaths and 2024 had 1. The data come from SES boletim and Sinan, highlighting a rising weekly case trend in contrast to 2025.",
