        ],
        "articleSummary": "Pernambuco opens 38 new pediatric beds to address a seasonal surge in respiratory viruses, with 8 pediatric ICU beds at Hospital Barão de Lucena in Recife, 20 ward beds at Hospital de Jaboatão Prazeres in Jaboatão dos Guararapes, and 10 ward beds at Hospital Otávio de Freitas. The expansion targets care as influenza and Respiratory Syncytial Virus (RSV) circulate, predominantly affecting children under two. The Barão de Lucena ICU pediatric sector was refurbished and relaunched this week, integrated into the State Regulation Center. SES-PE teams meet weekly to monitor epidemiology and strategies to reduce health-system pressure. Up to Epidemiological Week 9 of 2026, Pernambuco registered 702 Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome (Srag) cases, including 331 in 0–2-year-olds; in 2025, 7,375 Srag cases were recorded, 54.7% in the same age group.",
