        "articleSummary": "Yellow fever alerts persist in South America as PAHO reports sustained transmission and geographic expansion beyond the Amazon basin. Since late 2024, cases have emerged in areas previously free, including zones outside the Amazon. In 2025, the region logged 346 confirmed cases and 143 deaths. In the first seven weeks of 2026, 34 human cases and 15 deaths were reported, concentrated mainly in Bolivia, Colombia, Peru, and Venezuela, with Peru and Venezuela currently leading transmission. PAHO urges intensified vaccination for vulnerable populations and high-risk areas, strengthened epidemiological surveillance for early outbreak detection, and traveler guidance on vaccine requirements or recommendations before entering high-risk zones. Critical to reducing mortality is timely clinical management; states should maintain strategic vaccine reserves and bolster emergency department capacity to treat severe yellow fever complications.",
