        "articleSummary": "On 14 March 2026, Guarulhos, Brazil, authorities urge residents to inspect homes for Aedes aegypti breeding sites, the vectors of dengue, Zika, and chikungunya. Most foci occur indoors, so population participation is essential to interrupt transmission. Key steps: seal water tanks and reservoirs; regularly clean refrigerator and air-conditioning trays; keep exterior drains clear and screened; close rarely used toilets. Store bottles mouth-down; stretch tarps to prevent puddles; empty outdoor toys. Check roofs for depressions after rain and ensure proper drainage; keep gutters clear. Plant pot saucers should contain sand to prevent water accumulation; wash pet bowls frequently. In outdoor areas, treat and cover pools when unused. About ten minutes of weekly checks in yards, balconies, and service areas can eliminate most breeding sites and protect public health zonal.",
