        "articleSummary": "Viçosa, Brazil, hosted a dengue-control training for representatives from about 30 municipalities in the Ponte Nova region, including Araponga, Cajuri, Canaã, Paula Cândido, Pedra do Anta, Porto Firme, São Miguel do Anta, and Teixeiras. The aim was to strengthen arboviral surveillance and vector-control actions, standardizing teams for rapid response to suspected or confirmed cases. The two-day program began March 10 at the Salão Nobre Professor Arduino Bolivar, focusing on criteria for Ultra Low Volume (fumacê) applications, safe procedures for workers and residents, and integrated epidemiological surveillance strategies against Aedes aegypti, the principal vector of dengue, Zika, and chikungunya. A practical session followed on March 11 in the Bom Jesus neighborhood for logistical convenience near the city hall. Attendees included Dionísio Paccelli Costa (CEVARB, SES/MG arboviruses), Raimundo Nato Moreira (SES/MG Arboviruses), Graziele Dias (Vigilance Coord., SRS/PN), Geraldo Souza Caudas (SRSPN), and Lilian Souza (Viçosa Health Surveillance).",
