        "articleSummary": "In Hyderabad, Telangana, a young woman who refused an engagement was allegedly injected with an HIV-contaminated needle by a local man, prompting a police case within the Bacharam police station limits. After developing fever, she tested HIV-positive; investigators found the accused and several family members are also HIV-positive. The man, named Manohar, was arrested and remanded to judicial custody. The victim is receiving antiretroviral therapy and counseling. The March 11, 2026 incident involved the assailant pressuring her to marry and forcibly visiting her home, during which the needle injection occurred before he fled. Authorities are pursuing the case and providing necessary medical care to the patient.",
