        "articleSummary": "Yellow fever is experiencing sustained transmission in parts of South America, with cases continuing in 2026 and detections beyond traditional Amazon Basin foci. Since September 2024, the Pan American Health Organization has reported outbreaks in areas previously spared, including locations outside the Amazon. PAHO urges member states to strengthen epidemiological surveillance, intensify vaccination campaigns for at-risk populations, and ensure travelers to areas where vaccination is recommended are informed and protected. Health systems should boost capacities for early detection and timely management of severe cases, and maintain strategic vaccine reserves to rapidly respond to outbreaks. In 2025, 346 confirmed cases and 143 deaths were recorded across seven countries: Bolivia (8/2), Brazil (120/48), Colombia (125/46), Ecuador (11/8), Peru (49/19), Venezuela (32/19), with Guyana not detailed in the report.",
