        "articleSummary": "A dengue prevention drive was conducted in Presidente Juscelino, Minas Gerais, Brazil, led by the municipal health team and endemic agents to intensify control efforts. Triggered by the rainy season and high temperatures that favor Aedes aegypti, the mutirão de limpeza involved cleaning public areas and educating residents on eliminating standing-water breeding sites. Residents were urged to remove water-collecting containers at homes and yards, such as bottles, tires, cans, and uncovered boxes. The administration emphasizes that community participation is essential to keep the city safer and reduce dengue case risk, highlighting the ongoing work of endemias agents and health workers in disease prevention and population wellbeing. The initiative aims to strengthen prevention measures and lower dengue risk in the municipality.",
