        "articleSummary": "Human Papillomavirus (HPV) vaccine dosing guidelines: 0.5 mL intramuscular. For ages 9–14, a two-dose series at 0 and 6–12 months with a minimum 5-month interval; if a dose is given <5 months after the prior, an extra dose is recommended. For individuals aged ≥15, a three-dose series at 0, 1–2 months, and 6 months; minimum intervals are 4 weeks between doses 1 and 2, 12 weeks between doses 2 and 3, and 5 months between doses 1 and 3; if the second or third dose is given too early, dosing should be repeated. Adults aged 27–45 may complete either a 2-dose series (if started at 9–14) or a 3-dose series (if started at ≥15) based on shared clinical decision-making. Immunocompromised individuals, including those with HIV, may receive the 3-dose series regardless of age. These guidelines are from the MSD Manual Professional Edition as of 2026-03-14.",
