        "articleSummary": "Acre, Brazil, recorded 1,002 probable dengue cases in 2026 through week 9, a 78.6% drop from 4,683 in the same period of 2025. Despite the decline, Acre ranks third nationally in incidence with a coefficient of 113.3, behind Tocantins (419.0) and Goiás (388.1). No dengue deaths have been reported in Acre so far in 2026; in the corresponding 2025 period there were 3 deaths with an incidence coefficient of 529.5. Lethality among probable cases in 2025 was 0.06%, while among severe cases it reached 11.11%. The case gender split is 53% male and 47% female. Dengue is transmitted by Aedes aegypti, breeding in standing water. Health authorities advise eliminating water-collecting containers, cleaning gutters, and ensuring water tanks are well sealed to curb mosquito reproduction.",
