        "articleSummary": "13 measles cases detected in Madiun City, East Java, in early 2026, according to the Madiun City Health Office (Dinkes PPKB). In 2025, 27 cases were recorded; January–February 2026 added 13 cases. The health office promotes vaccination, including catch-up immunization for infants aged 9–19 months who have not received the measles vaccine. In 2025, measles vaccination coverage reached 99.66% of the target (exceeding 95%); January–February 2026 coverage was 16.33%. The department targets 97% vaccination in 2026. Citizens are urged to seek care if symptomatic, with measles presenting as fever followed by a red rash, especially in children. Measles can cause diarrhea with dehydration, pneumonia, encephalitis, blindness, or death. Besides vaccination, emphasize hygiene (handwashing with soap), masking when ill, and nutritious diet; Lebaran 2026 travel may raise transmission risk, necessitating vigilance.",
