        "articleSummary": "March 2026: Dourados, Brazil expands tuberculosis control through intensified screening and early-diagnosis efforts led by the Municipal Health Secretariat and the Center for Reference in Tuberculosis and Leprosy (CRTH), in partnership with Primary Health Units and the Health Surveillance Department. The campaign, aligned with World Tuberculosis Day on March 24, includes educational activities, active case finding among people with respiratory symptoms, and expanded diagnostic testing. SINAN data show rising TB notifications in Dourados, from 192 cases in 2024 to 258 in 2025. TB is an airborne infectious disease caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis, primarily affecting the lungs, with symptoms such as cough lasting more than three weeks, low-grade afternoon fever, night sweats, weight loss, and fatigue. High-risk groups include the elderly, diabetics, indigenous communities, institutionalized individuals, and immunocompromised persons. Prison and semi-open regime units will bolster case identification and laboratory access, supporting national targets.",
