        "articleSummary": "Liaoning Province CDC warns of spring-era respiratory and enteric infections in China as of 2026-03-14. Measles remains highly contagious; symptoms start with fever, cough, and runny nose, followed by facial rash that spreads to the body. Incubation 7–21 days; infectious period spans from five days before to five days after rash. Two-dose MMR vaccination is essential; ensure catch-up for unvaccinated children. Parotitis (mumps) also poses outbreak risk in schools; symptoms include fever and swollen salivary glands, with vaccination via two-dose MMR recommended and strict infection prevention in facilities. Respiratory infections overall are still active; RSV, rhinovirus, and SARS-CoV-2 circulate; emphasize masks, hand hygiene, ventilation, and prompt medical care for fever or respiratory symptoms. Norovirus/Rotavirus-linked gastroenteritis calls for strict handwashing, food-safety, disinfection, and dehydration management. Brucellosis risk rises with lambing season in spring; avoid direct contact with infected livestock, use PPE, and ensure cooking of meat. Hepatitis A concerns persist in coastal areas; vaccinate at-risk groups and enforce safe seafood handling and water hygiene.",
