        "articleSummary": "Measles activity in Indonesia shows a national downturn in suspected cases (10,826) and confirmed cases (8,716) through week 9 of 2026, after a January uptick, with 45 outbreaks (KLB) in 29 districts/cities across 11 provinces. Lab confirmation occurs in 11 provinces; NTB (Bima Regency and Bima City) remains high with 544 suspected and 476 confirmed cases. Despite the decline, officials urge parents to monitor children during Lebaran travel and delay trips if fever, rash, cough, runny nose, or red eyes appear, given measles’ high contagion (12–18 others). PHBS measures include masks for respiratory symptoms and in crowded places, plus handwashing. ORI MR immunization underway in 22 districts/cities; two districts not yet started after KLB. CuC MR immunization is highest in Jakarta Barat 56.4%, Jakarta Pusat 80.4%, Depok 17.3%, Tangerang Selatan 8.4%, Palu 5.6%. Immunization services at Puskesmas/Posyandu and Mudik points; parents should verify MR vaccination at 9 and 18 months.",
