        "articleSummary": "Dengue fever remains a serious threat in Indonesia. The United Against Dengue (UAD): Joint Initiative to Fight Dengue campaign was launched in Jakarta by Takeda Innovative Medicines, the International Federation of Red Cross and Red Crescent Societies (IFRC), and the Indonesian Red Cross (PMI). Indonesia is the first country to activate the national partnership, following a regional UAD launch in June 2025. The campaign aims to strengthen prevention, preparedness and community-based interventions through multi-sector collaboration, evidence-based strategies and innovations to reduce transmission and disease severity. Takeda's Andreas Gutknecht emphasized the goal of zero dengue deaths by 2030; IFRC's Kathryn Clarkson highlighted building community resilience; PMI’s Fachmi Idris connected the effort to national dengue-control strategies. Dengue is transmitted by Aedes aegypti; WHO reported 14.6 million cases and 12,000 deaths worldwide in 2024. In 2024, Indonesia’s BPJS Kesehatan recorded 1,055,255 dengue hospitalizations, with nearly Rp 3 trillion in economic burden.",
