        "articleSummary": "An HIV-positive man was arrested in Telangana's Medchal-Malkajgiri district for allegedly injecting his own HIV-positive blood into a 24-year-old woman after her family called off the marriage. The incident occurred in Ghatkesar town when the man forced a syringe of his blood into the woman. The accused is a close relative; his HIV status was confirmed six months earlier in a lab in Uppal when the father had him tested after the marriage was called off. The woman was taken to a private hospital in Uppal and later shifted to Gandhi Hospital for treatment. The police arrested him on Saturday and he was remanded to 14 days judicial custody; the investigation is ongoing.",
